        "original_id": "a1c89219-4e32-51e3-b7bc-388588c02c60",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Songs: \"Friends in Low Places\", \"Mr. Blue\", \"I'm Gonna Hire a Wino to Decorate Our Home\"\n- People: Garth Brooks, Dewayne Blackwell, David Frizzell\n- Albums: \"No Fences\"\n- Groups: the Fleetwoods\n- Charts: Billboard Top Country Albums\n\nFacts:\n- \"Mr. Blue\" was a 1959 hit song for the Fleetwoods, and Dewayne Blackwell wrote it.\n- \"I'm Gonna Hire a Wino to Decorate Our Home\" was a 1982 hit song for David Frizzell, and Dewayne Blackwell wrote it.\n- \"Friends in Low Places\" is a song performed by American country pop artist Garth Brooks.\n- \"Friends in Low Places\" was released on August 6, 1990 as the lead single from Garth Brooks's album \"No Fences\".\n- \"Friends in Low Places\" was a 1990 hit song for Garth Brooks, and Dewayne Blackwell wrote it.\n- \"No Fences\" was released on August 27, 1990.\n- \"No Fences\" reached number 1 on Billboard's Top Country Albums chart.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
